# Why: A recommendation that contradicted an earlier settled decision (a public series ID used as a join permission) survived four rounds in the File Drawer design; a cold read by a fresh sub-agent of the written decisions is the check the per-round flow lacks.
# Why: Recommendations must be checked against the repo's written rules and the code before they're offered: a filedrawer session recommended rewriting applied migrations, which CODING_STANDARDS forbids, and a SQL publish the code can't do
--- a/SKILL.md
